hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"282","We are Nasr bin Marzuq, we are Asad, meaning the son of Musa. H Muhammad bin Amr bin Tammam Al-Masry narrated to us, Ali bin Ma’bad narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Al-Muharriq, on the authority of Lubaba bint Al-Harith, she said: Al-Hussein urinated on the lap of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said: Bring your dress, bring it. He washed it, and he said: “It is only washed with female urine, and sprinkled with male urine.”"
"283","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told me, Abdul-Rahman bin Mahdi told me, Yahya bin Al-Walid told me, Mahal bin Khalifa Al-Tai told me, He said: Abu Al-Samh told me, he said: I was the servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he brought Al-Hasan, or Al-Hussein, and he urinated on his chest, so they wanted to They washed him, and he said: “Sprinkle him with a sprinkle, for he is washed with the urine of a female slave and sprinkled with the urine of a boy.”"
